#
# Why this exists:
#   react-native-worklets "bundle mode" isolates each worklet into a throwaway module
#   (node_modules/react-native-worklets/.worklets/*.js) at build time. Metro does not
#   index these generated files in time, so bundling fails with
#   "Failed to get the SHA-1 for: .../react-native-worklets/.worklets/<hash>.js".
#   This patch makes Metro return a pseudo-SHA-1 for anything under the .worklets dir.
#
# This is the officially-provided workaround from Software Mansion
# (react-native-worklets bundleMode docs), a stopgap until the fix is merged into Metro.
#
# REMOVAL TRIGGER: Drop this patch once either:
#   1. A future Expo SDK (e.g. 58+) bundles a Metro that ships the SHA-1 index fix natively, OR
#   2. An SDK-57-compatible Metro (pinned by @expo/metro@56.0.0 -> metro@0.84.4)
#      releases the fix without requiring a package bump.
#
# CAUTION: We are pinned to metro@0.84.4 by Expo SDK 57. The "latest" Metro tag (0.87.x)
#   is NOT usable here - upgrading Metro without a matching SDK breaks the Expo Go pin.
#   Do NOT appease this TODO by bumping metro to a later tag.
#
# When considering removal, re-check the upstream patches folder for what SDK 57 supports:
#   https://github.com/software-mansion/react-native-reanimated/tree/main/packages/react-native-worklets/bundleMode/patches/patch-package/metro

